[{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"<table style=\"width:100%; border:none; border-collapse:collapse;\">\n  <tr>\n    <td style=\"width:12%; border:none;\"></td>\n    <td style=\"width:38%; text-align:center; vertical-align:middle; border:none;\">\n      <img src=\"./OperationNextNest.png\" style=\"width:410px;\"/>\n    </td>\n    <td style=\"width:38%; text-align:center; vertical-align:middle; border:none;\">\n      <img src=\"./OperationNextNest2.png\" style=\"width:280px;\"/>\n    </td>\n    <td style=\"width:12%; border:none;\"></td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\n---\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n\n## 🏡 Operation Next Nest | Part 2 | Neighborhood Scoring in SAS\n\n</div>\n\n---","outputs":[]},{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"<div style=\"background-color:#e8f1fb; padding:0; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid #c7dff7;\">\n\n<div style=\"background-color:#1f77b4; color:white; padding:10px 16px; border-top-left-radius:8px; border-top-right-radius:8px;\">\n<b>Operation Next Nest | Project Overview</b>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"padding:16px;\">\n\nThis project follows a simple question:\n\n> **Where should Lincoln and his family look for their next home near SAS headquarters in Cary, North Carolina?**\n\nTo explore that question, we combine three analytics tools — each playing a different role in the workflow.\n\n| Tool | Role | Purpose |\n|-----|------|---------|\n| Python | Data Engineering | Build the neighborhood dataset |\n| SAS | Scenario Comparison | Evaluate neighborhoods under different priorities |\n| R | Interactive Mapping | Visualize geographic patterns and robust candidates |\n\nTogether, these steps create a complete **data → decision → insight** pipeline for exploring real-world choices.\n\n</div>\n</div>","outputs":[]},{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"Welcome back to **Part 2 of Operation Next Nest**. It's time to dive deeper into the data!\n\nIn **Part 1 (Python)**, we assembled the raw ingredients needed to evaluate neighborhoods. Using publicly available data sources, we built a dataset containing:\n\n- Estimated commute time to SAS  \n- Housing affordability measures  \n- Local economic indicators  \n- Indicators for kid-friendly neighborhoods  \n- Access to nearby amenities such as parks, grocery stores, and bike trails  \n\nBy the end of Part 1, we had transformed a collection of raw geographic and census data into a **structured dataset of candidate neighborhoods**.\n\nMission accomplished… at least for the **data engineering** phase.\n\nBut assembling the data is only half the challenge.\n\nNow we face the real question:\n\n> **Which neighborhoods best balance everything that matters to Lincoln’s family?**\n\nSome neighborhoods might offer shorter commutes.  \nOthers may have stronger local economies or newer housing.  \nOthers might provide more parks, trails, or family-friendly amenities.\n\nChoosing between them requires a **structured way to compare tradeoffs**.\n\n---\n\n## Mission Objective: A Structured Neighborhood Comparison\n\nIn this notebook, we will use SAS to build a **transparent scoring framework** that allows us to compare neighborhoods across multiple priorities.\n\nYou will occasionally see the word **optimization**, because we will use the SAS optimization language (`PROC OPTMODEL`) to implement the scoring framework.\n\nHowever, the goal here is not advanced mathematics.\n\nInstead, our goal is to create a **clear and structured way to compare neighborhood options** based on what matters most to Lincoln’s household.\n\nThink of this notebook as building a **decision comparison tool**, not solving a purely mathematical optimization problem.\n\n---\n\n## What We Will Do in This Notebook\n\nIn this mission, we will:\n\n1. Build a **scoring system** for neighborhoods  \n2. Define different **“what matters most?” scenarios**  \n3. Use SAS to identify the **Top 10 candidate neighborhoods**  \n4. Explore how **changing priorities changes the results**\n\nOur scoring framework will consider several dimensions:\n\n- Commute time  \n- Housing value  \n- Local economic indicators  \n- Family-friendly demographics  \n- Neighborhood amenities  \n\nEach factor contributes to an overall **neighborhood desirability score**.\n\nThe weights we assign to these factors represent **what matters most to Lincoln’s family**.\n\nChanging those weights will often change which neighborhoods rise to the top.\n\nThis highlights an important lesson in analytics:\n\n> There is rarely a single “correct” answer — only better decisions given your priorities.\n\n---\n\n## Why SAS for This Step?\n\nOnce the data has been prepared, the problem becomes a **structured decision comparison problem**.\n\nWe want to evaluate many neighborhoods simultaneously while balancing multiple criteria.\n\nSAS provides powerful decision modeling tools, including **PROC OPTMODEL**, which allow us to:\n\n- Define scoring formulas  \n- Apply constraints (such as maximum commute time)  \n- Compare many alternatives simultaneously  \n- Identify the highest-scoring candidate neighborhoods  \n\nIn other words, SAS helps us turn data into a **transparent scoring framework** for comparing neighborhoods.\n\n---\n\n## Why SAS Viya Workbench Helps\n\nOne advantage of working in **SAS Viya Workbench** is that multiple programming languages can operate within the same shared analytics environment.\n\nIn Part 1, **Python** performed the data engineering and feature creation.\n\nNow, in Part 2, **SAS** can immediately consume that dataset and apply decision modeling techniques.\n\nThere are:\n\n- No manual exports  \n- No file transfers  \n- No switching platforms  \n\nJust a **seamless workflow across Python and SAS within the same analytics environment**.\n\n---\n\n**Mission briefing complete.**\n\nLet’s load the dataset from Part 1 and begin evaluating Lincoln’s candidate neighborhoods.\n\n---","outputs":[]},{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"### Step 1 | Load the Dataset\n\nWe begin by loading the dataset created in Part 1. Because all work is performed within the same SAS Viya Workbench environment, SAS can immediately access the file produced in Python. This creates a seamless transition from data engineering to neighborhood comparison.","outputs":[]},{"kind":2,"language":"sas","value":"/*--------------------------------------------------------------*\n | Step 1 | Load the Operation Next Nest data from Part 1\n |\n | Note:\n | The dataset created in Python is stored in the shared\n | workspace so SAS can read it directly. If your folder\n | structure differs, update the path below as needed.\n *--------------------------------------------------------------*/\n\n/* Point SAS to the shared project folder */\n%let proj_root = &WORKSPACE_PATH./OperationNextNest;\n%let data_path = &proj_root./Data;\n\n/* Import the CSV created in Part 1 */\nproc import datafile=\"&data_path./operation_next_nest.csv\"\n    out=work.operation_next_nest_raw\n    dbms=csv\n    replace;\n    guessingrows=max;\nrun;\n\n/* Take a quick look at the imported data */\ntitle \"Structure of the imported Operation Next Nest dataset\";\nproc contents data=work.operation_next_nest_raw order=varnum;\nrun;\n\ntitle \"First 5 observations from the imported dataset\";\nproc print data=work.operation_next_nest_raw(obs=5);\nrun;\n\ntitle;","outputs":[{"items":[{"data":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\" xml:lang=\"en\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\"/>\n<meta content=\"SAS V.04.00\" name=\"generator\"/>\n<title>SAS Output</title>\n<style>\n/*<![CDATA[*/\n.body.c > table, .body.c > pre, .body.c div > table,\n.body.c div > pre, .body.c > table, .body.c > pre,\n.body.j > table, .body.j > pre, .body.j div > table,\n.body.j div > pre, .body.j > table, .body.j > pre,\n.body.c p.note, .body.c p.warning, .body.c p.error, .body.c p.fatal,\n.body.j p.note, .body.j p.warning, .body.j p.error, .body.j p.fatal,\n.body.c > table.layoutcontainer, .body.j > table.layoutcontainer { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto }\n.layoutregion.l table, .layoutregion.l pre, .layoutregion.l p.note,\n.layoutregion.l p.warning, .layoutregion.l p.error, .layoutregion.l p.fatal { margin-left: 0 }\n.layoutregion.c table, .layoutregion.c pre, .layoutregion.c p.note,\n.layoutregion.c p.warning, .layoutregion.c p.error, .layoutregion.c p.fatal { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto }\n.layoutregion.r table, .layoutregion.r pre, .layoutregion.r p.note,\n.layoutregion.r table, .layoutregion.r pre, .layoutregion.r p.note,\n.layoutregion.r p.warning, .layoutregion.r p.error, .layoutregion.r p.fatal { margin-right: 0 }\narticle, aside, details, figcaption, figure, footer, header, hgroup, nav, section { display: block }\nhtml{ font-size: 100% }\n.body { margin: 1em; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.231 }\nsup { position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; bottom: 0.25em; font-size: 0.8em }\nsub { position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: 0.25em; font-size: 0.8em }\nul, ol { margin: 1em 0; padding: 0 0 0 40px }\ndd { margin: 0 0 0 40px }\nnav ul, nav ol { list-style: none; list-style-image: none; margin: 0; padding: 0 }\nimg { border: 0; vertical-align: middle }\nsvg:not(:root) { overflow: hidden }\nfigure { margin: 0 }\ntable { border-collapse: collapse; border-spacing: 0 }\n.layoutcontainer { border-collapse: separate; border-spacing: 0 }\np { margin-top: 0; text-align: left }\nh1.heading1 { text-align: left }\nh2.heading2 { text-align: left }\nh3.heading3 { text-align: left }\nh4.heading4 { text-align: left }\nh5.heading5 { text-align: left }\nh6.heading6 { text-align: left }\nspan { text-align: left }\ntable { margin-bottom: 1em }\ntd, th { text-align: left; padding: 3px 6px; vertical-align: top }\ntd[class$=\"fixed\"], th[class$=\"fixed\"] { white-space: pre }\nsection, article { padding-top: 1px; padding-bottom: 8px }\nhr.pagebreak { height: 0px; border: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #c0c0c0; margin: 1em 0 }\n.stacked-value { text-align: left; display: block }\n.stacked-cell > .stacked-value, td.data > td.data, th.data > td.data, th.data > th.data, td.data > th.data, th.header > th.header { border: 0 }\n.stacked-cell > div.data { border-width: 0 }\n.systitleandfootercontainer { white-space: nowrap; margin-bottom: 1em }\n.systitleandfootercontainer > p { margin: 0 }\n.systitleandfootercontainer > p > span { display: inline-block; width: 100%; white-space: normal }\n.batch { display: table }\n.toc { display: none }\n.proc_note_group, .proc_title_group { margin-bottom: 1em }\np.proctitle { margin: 0 }\np.note, p.warning, p.error, p.fatal { display: table }\n.notebanner, .warnbanner, .errorbanner, .fatalbanner,\n.notecontent, .warncontent, .errorcontent, .fatalcontent { display: table-cell; padding: 0.5em }\n.notebanner, .warnbanner, .errorbanner, .fatalbanner { padding-right: 0 }\n.body > div > ol li { text-align: left }\n.beforecaption > h4 { margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0 }\n.c { text-align: center }\n.r { text-align: right }\n.l { text-align: left }\n.j { text-align: justify }\n.d { text-align: right }\n.b { vertical-align: bottom }\n.m { vertical-align: middle }\n.t { vertical-align: top }\n.accessiblecaption {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 11pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\na:active { color: #800080 }\n.aftercaption {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-spacing: 0;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    padding-top: 4pt;\n}\n.batch > colgroup {\n    border-left: 1px solid #c1c1c1;\n    border-right: 1px solid #c1c1c1;\n}\n.batch > tbody, .batch > thead, .batch > tfoot {\n    border-top: 1px solid #c1c1c1;\n    border-bottom: 1px solid #c1c1c1;\n}\n.batch { border: hidden; }\n.batch {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border: 1px solid #c1c1c1;\n    border-collapse: separate;\n    border-spacing: 1px;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'SAS Monospace', 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\n    font-size: 7pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    padding: 7px;\n    }\n.beforecaption {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-spacing: 0;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.body {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    margin-left: 8px;\n    margin-right: 8px;\n}\n.bodydate {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-spacing: 0;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    text-align: right;\n    vertical-align: top;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.bycontentfolder {\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    list-style-type: none;\n    margin-left: 6pt;\n}\n.byline {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-spacing: 0;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.bylinecontainer > col, .bylinecontainer > colgroup > col, .bylinecontainer > colgroup, .bylinecontainer > tr, .bylinecontainer > * > tr, .bylinecontainer > thead, .bylinecontainer > tbody, .bylinecontainer > tfoot { border: none; }\n.bylinecontainer {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border: none;\n    border-spacing: 1px;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.caption {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-spacing: 0;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.cell, .container {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.contentfolder, .contentitem {\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    list-style-type: none;\n    margin-left: 6pt;\n}\n.contentproclabel, .contentprocname {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 11pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.contents {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    list-style-type: decimal;\n    margin-left: 8px;\n    margin-right: 8px;\n}\n.contentsdate {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.contenttitle {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.continued {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-spacing: 0;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.data, .dataemphasis {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #c1c1c1;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.dataemphasisfixed {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #c1c1c1;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\n    font-size: 8pt;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.dataempty {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #c1c1c1;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.datafixed {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #c1c1c1;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier;\n    font-size: 8pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.datastrong {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #c1c1c1;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.datastrongfixed {\n    background-color: #ffffff;\n    border-color: #c1c1c1;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier, monospace;\n    font-size: 8pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.date {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n.document {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.errorbanner {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.errorcontent {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.errorcontentfixed {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier;\n    font-size: 8pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.extendedpage {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 1pt;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    text-align: center;\n}\n.fatalbanner {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n.fatalcontent {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.fatalcontentfixed {\n    background-color: #fafbfe;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Courier New', Courier;\n    font-size: 8pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n}\n.folderaction {\n    color: #000000;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 9pt;\n    font-style: normal;\n    font-weight: normal;\n    list-style-type: none;\n    margin-left: 6pt;\n}\n.footer {\n    background-color: #edf2f9;\n    border-color: #b0b7bb;\n    border-style: solid;\n    border-width: 0 1px 1px 0;\n    color: #112277;\n    font-family: 'Anova UI', Arial, 'Albany AMT', Helvetica, Helv;\n    font-size: 