,\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"      real time           0.06 seconds\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"note\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"      cpu time            0.09 seconds\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"note\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"      \",\n\t\t\"type\": \"note\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"note\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"1895  ;*';*\\\";*/;run;quit;ods html5(id=vscode) close;\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"source\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"1896  \",\n\t\t\"type\": \"source\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t},\n\t{\n\t\t\"line\": \"\",\n\t\t\"type\": \"note\",\n\t\t\"version\": 1\n\t}\n]","mime":"application/vnd.sas.compute.log.lines"}]}]},{"kind":1,"language":"markdown","value":"***\n\n## Part 2 Complete | Scenario-Based Neighborhood Comparison\n\nNice work — this was the **decision modeling phase** of Operation Next Nest.\n\nIn this notebook, you:\n\n✔ Built a structured scoring framework for comparing neighborhoods  \n✔ Applied practical constraints such as commute time and housing value  \n✔ Explored how **different priorities lead to different recommendations**  \n✔ Generated scenario results that can be visualized and compared\n\nRather than producing a single “perfect” answer, the goal was to identify **strong candidate neighborhoods under different preference scenarios**.\n\nThis reflects an important lesson in analytics:\n\n> Good models don’t replace decisions — they help clarify the tradeoffs.\n\n### Key Takeaways\n\n- There is rarely **one perfect neighborhood**\n- Changing priorities leads to **different high-scoring candidates**\n- Structured comparison helps make decision tradeoffs **more transparent**\n\n### Where We Are in the Workflow\n\nSo far in **Operation Next Nest** we have used:\n\n| Part | Tool | Purpose |\n|-----|------|---------|\n| Part 1 | Python | Build and engineer the neighborhood dataset |\n| Part 2 | SAS (`PROC OPTMODEL`) | Compare neighborhoods under different scenarios |\n| Part 3 | R | Visualize the results geographically |\n\n### Up Next: Part 3 — Neighborhood Maps in R\n\nIn Part 3, we will bring these results to life using interactive maps.\n\nWe’ll explore:\n\n- Where each scenario leads us geographically  \n- Which neighborhoods appear in **multiple scenarios**  \n- Where the most promising areas are for real-world house hunting\n\nIn the next notebook, we’ll load the scenario results and explore them geographically using R.","outputs":[]}]